  "worked_solution": "To compute ${a}_{4},$ we first need to compute ${a}_{3}.$ So, we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+2} & ={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n} \\\\ {a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-1+(-3) \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to compute ${a}_{4},$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2+2} & ={a}_{2+1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-4+(-1) \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{4}=-5.$",
